IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bnra-types`
IMPORT `bnra-part2-registration`

-- Tests for Part 2, ss 5 to 14.  Thresholds read off the text: 30 days to appeal (ss 8(7),
-- 12(4)); at least 30 days for representations (s 12(3)) and for renewal (s 14(2)); 30
-- days to appoint an authorised representative (s 11(4), (11)); 14 days for the notices in
-- s 11(7) and (9); age 18 (s 11(2)).  #TRACE results are printed, not asserted; NOTES.md
-- records them.

§ `Tests -- Part 2, ss 5 to 14`

§§ `5. Requirement to register`

--                                     carries on business, person registered, name registered, business names, separate registrations
`registered in full` MEANS `Registration Requirement Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  1, 1
`not registered at all` MEANS `Registration Requirement Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, 1, 0
`registered but not the name` MEANS `Registration Requirement Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, 1, 1
`not carrying on business` MEANS `Registration Requirement Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, 1, 0
`two names, one registration` MEANS `Registration Requirement Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  2, 1
`two names, two registrations` MEANS `Registration Requirement Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  2, 2

#ASSERT `the person and the business name were registered before the person carried on business` `registered in full` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person and the business name were registered before the person carried on business` `not registered at all` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the person and the business name were registered before the person carried on business` `registered but not the name` TRUE
#ASSERT `the person and the business name were registered before the person carried on business` `not registered at all` FALSE
#ASSERT `the person and the business name were registered before the person carried on business` `not carrying on business` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `there is a separate registration for each business name` `two names, one registration`
#ASSERT `there is a separate registration for each business name` `two names, two registrations`
#ASSERT `there is a separate registration for each business name` `registered in full`

§§ `6. Manner and particulars of registration`

--                                       full name, identification, nationality, residential address, contact address
`complete particulars` MEANS `Personal Particulars` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`particulars without a nationality` MEANS `Personal Particulars` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`particulars without a contact address` MEANS `Personal Particulars` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the personal particulars are complete` `complete particulars`
#ASSERT NOT `the personal particulars are complete` `particulars without a nationality`
#ASSERT NOT `the personal particulars are complete` `particulars without a contact address`

-- Application Facts: kind, lodged, by an appropriate person, business name, general nature,
-- principal place, commencement date, individual proprietor's particulars, sole proprietor's
-- corporate details, every individual partner's particulars, every corporate partner's
-- details, every authorised representative's particulars, other prescribed information.
`a complete individual proprietor application` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`an individual proprietor application without a contact address` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `particulars without a contact address`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`an application without a business name` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`an application without a general nature` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`an application without a principal place` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`an application without a commencement date` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`an application without the other prescribed information` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, FALSE
`a company sole proprietor application with its corporate details` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `a company that is a sole proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `particulars without a nationality`, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`a company sole proprietor application without its corporate details` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `a company that is a sole proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`a firm application with complete partners` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `a firm`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `particulars without a nationality`, FALSE, (LIST `complete particulars`, `complete particulars`), TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`a firm application with an incomplete partner` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `a firm`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `particulars without a nationality`, FALSE, (LIST `complete particulars`, `particulars without a contact address`), TRUE, EMPTY, TRUE
`a firm application without its corporate partners' details` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `a firm`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `particulars without a nationality`, FALSE, (LIST `complete particulars`), FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE
`an application with a complete authorised representative` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, (LIST `complete particulars`), TRUE
`an application with an incomplete authorised representative` MEANS `Application Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, `complete particulars`, FALSE, EMPTY, TRUE, (LIST `particulars without a nationality`), TRUE

#ASSERT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `a complete individual proprietor application`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an individual proprietor application without a contact address`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an application without a business name`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an application without a general nature`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an application without a principal place`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an application without a commencement date`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an application without the other prescribed information`
#ASSERT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `a company sole proprietor application with its corporate details`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `a company sole proprietor application without its corporate details`
#ASSERT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `a firm application with complete partners`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `a firm application with an incomplete partner`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `a firm application without its corporate partners' details`
#ASSERT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an application with a complete authorised representative`
#ASSERT NOT `the application contains the particulars section 6(1)(b) requires` `an application with an incomplete authorised representative`

-- 6(3): the appropriate person
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `an individual proprietor` `the individual proprietor`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an appropriate person` `an individual proprietor` `a director or a secretary of the company`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a company that is a sole proprietor` `a director or a secretary of the company`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an appropriate person` `a company that is a sole proprietor` `a manager of the limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a limited liability partnership that is a sole proprietor` `a manager of the limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a foreign company that is a sole proprietor` `an authorised representative of the foreign company, as section 366 of the Companies Act 1967 defines it`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a firm` `a partner of the firm who is an individual`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a firm` `a director or a secretary of a company that is a partner of the firm`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a firm` `a manager of a limited liability partnership that is a partner of the firm`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a firm` `an authorised representative of a foreign company that is a partner of the firm`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an appropriate person` `a firm` `the individual proprietor`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `an individual proprietor` `a registered corporate service provider authorised by and acting for the person`
#ASSERT `the person is an appropriate person` `a firm` `a registered corporate service provider authorised by and acting for the person`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an appropriate person` `a firm` `someone else`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an appropriate person` `an individual proprietor` `someone else`
#ASSERT `the application is properly lodged` `a complete individual proprietor application` `the individual proprietor`
#ASSERT NOT `the application is properly lodged` `a complete individual proprietor application` `someone else`

§§ `7. Registration by nominee or trustee`

--                                       nominee/trustee, gave s 6 particulars, gave prescribed particulars, other person is a foreign company
`a nominee who gave everything` MEANS `Nominee Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a nominee who omitted the prescribed particulars` MEANS `Nominee Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a nominee who omitted the s 6 particulars` MEANS `Nominee Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`not a nominee` MEANS `Nominee Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a nominee of a foreign company` MEANS `Nominee Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE

#ASSERT `the nominee or trustee has provided the particulars section 7(1) requires` `a nominee who gave everything`
#ASSERT NOT `the nominee or trustee has provided the particulars section 7(1) requires` `a nominee who omitted the prescribed particulars`
#ASSERT NOT `the nominee or trustee has provided the particulars section 7(1) requires` `a nominee who omitted the s 6 particulars`
#ASSERT `the nominee or trustee has provided the particulars section 7(1) requires` `not a nominee`
#ASSERT `the person contravenes section 7(2)` `a nominee of a foreign company`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 7(2)` `a nominee who gave everything`
#ASSERT NOT `the person contravenes section 7(2)` `not a nominee`

§§ `8. Registration`

-- Registration Decision Facts: application received, satisfied with particulars, satisfied
-- unlawful purpose, satisfied contrary to national interest, foreign company, registered
-- under Division 2, name must be refused under s 17, Minister consents.
`no application yet` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an application in good order` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an application for an unlawful business` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an application contrary to national interest` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an application by an unregistered foreign company` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an application by a registered foreign company` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an application under a barred name` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`an application under a barred name with the Minister's consent` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`an application the Registrar is not satisfied with` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an unlawful application the Registrar is also not satisfied with` MEANS `Registration Decision Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `no application yet` EQUALS `there is no application to decide`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application in good order` EQUALS `the Registrar must register the applicant and the business name and issue a notice of registration`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application for an unlawful business` EQUALS `the Registrar must refuse to register`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application contrary to national interest` EQUALS `the Registrar must refuse to register`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application by an unregistered foreign company` EQUALS `the Registrar must refuse to register`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application by a registered foreign company` EQUALS `the Registrar must register the applicant and the business name and issue a notice of registration`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application under a barred name` EQUALS `the Registrar must refuse to register`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application under a barred name with the Minister's consent` EQUALS `the Registrar must register the applicant and the business name and issue a notice of registration`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an application the Registrar is not satisfied with` EQUALS `the Registrar is not required to register`
#ASSERT `the Registrar's duty on an application for registration` `an unlawful application the Registrar is also not satisfied with` EQUALS `the Registrar must refuse to register`

-- 8(2): certificate of confirmation.  Certificate Facts: registered, applied, fee paid.
#ASSERT `the Registrar may issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` (`Certificate Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` (`Certificate Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` (`Certificate Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may issue a certificate of confirmation of registration` (`Certificate Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)

-- 8(3), (4), (5): renewal.  Renewal Facts: applied, fee paid, Registrar asked for more,
-- more provided, Registrar satisfied.
#ASSERT `the registration is renewable` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the registration is renewable` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the registration is renewable` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may refuse to renew because additional particulars were not provided` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may refuse to renew because additional particulars were not provided` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the registration is renewable` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar is not required to renew the registration` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the registration is renewable` (`Renewal Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the registration is renewable` (`Renewal Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)

#ASSERT NOT `registration or renewal implies that the person has complied with the law relating to the business`

-- 8(7): appeal within 30 days.  Appeal Facts: aggrieved, date notified, date of appeal,
-- further date the Minister allowed, decision rests on the Minister's certificate.
`notified on 1 March 2026, appeal on the 30th day` MEANS `Appeal Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, NOTHING, FALSE
`notified on 1 March 2026, appeal on the 31st day` MEANS `Appeal Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 4 1, NOTHING, FALSE
`an appeal by a person not aggrieved` MEANS `Appeal Facts` OF FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 10, NOTHING, FALSE
`an appeal against a refusal resting on the certificate` MEANS `Appeal Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 10, NOTHING, TRUE
`late but within the further period the Minister allowed` MEANS `Appeal Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 5 15, JUST (YMD 2026 5 15), FALSE
`late and beyond the further period the Minister allowed` MEANS `Appeal Facts` OF TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 5 16, JUST (YMD 2026 5 15), FALSE

#ASSERT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` `notified on 1 March 2026, appeal on the 30th day`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` `notified on 1 March 2026, appeal on the 31st day`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` `an appeal by a person not aggrieved`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days` `an appeal against a refusal resting on the certificate`
-- 12(4): "or such further period as the Minister may allow"
#ASSERT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days or a further period the Minister allows` `notified on 1 March 2026, appeal on the 30th day`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days or a further period the Minister allows` `notified on 1 March 2026, appeal on the 31st day`
#ASSERT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days or a further period the Minister allows` `late but within the further period the Minister allowed`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days or a further period the Minister allows` `late and beyond the further period the Minister allowed`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may appeal to the Minister within 30 days or a further period the Minister allows` `an appeal against a refusal resting on the certificate`

§§ `9. When registration must be refused`

-- Public Interest Facts: satisfied unlawful purpose, satisfied contrary to national interest,
-- Minister's certificate.
`no concern` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an unlawful purpose` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a national interest concern` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a certificate only` MEANS `Public Interest Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse to register under section 9` `no concern` FALSE
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse to register under section 9` `an unlawful purpose` FALSE
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse to register under section 9` `a national interest concern` FALSE
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse to register under section 9` `a certificate only` FALSE
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse to register under section 9` `no concern` TRUE
#ASSERT `the certificate is conclusive evidence that it would be contrary to the national security or interest` `a certificate only`
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate is conclusive evidence that it would be contrary to the national security or interest` `no concern`

§§ `10. Registration does not confer ownership`

#ASSERT NOT `registration confers property in the registered business name or in a word in it`
#ASSERT NOT `registration is evidence that the person owns property or a right or interest in property used for the business`

§§ `11. Authorised representative`

--                                                       is a corporation, incorporated outside Singapore, residential address outside Singapore
`an individual living abroad` MEANS `Residence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`an individual living in Singapore` MEANS `Residence Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a corporation incorporated abroad` MEANS `Residence Facts` OF TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`a corporation incorporated in Singapore` MEANS `Residence Facts` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the person resides outside Singapore` `an individual living abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `the person resides outside Singapore` `an individual living in Singapore`
#ASSERT `the person resides outside Singapore` `a corporation incorporated abroad`
#ASSERT NOT `the person resides outside Singapore` `a corporation incorporated in Singapore`

#ASSERT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, (LIST `an individual living abroad`))
#ASSERT NOT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `an individual proprietor`, (LIST `an individual living in Singapore`))
#ASSERT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `a firm`, (LIST `an individual living abroad`, `a corporation incorporated abroad`))
#ASSERT NOT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `a firm`, (LIST `an individual living abroad`, `an individual living in Singapore`))
#ASSERT NOT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `a firm`, EMPTY)
#ASSERT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `a foreign company that is a sole proprietor`, (LIST `an individual living abroad`, `an individual living abroad`))
#ASSERT NOT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `a foreign company that is a sole proprietor`, (LIST `an individual living abroad`, `an individual living in Singapore`))
#ASSERT NOT `an authorised representative must be appointed` (`Representative Requirement Facts` OF `a company that is a sole proprietor`, (LIST `a corporation incorporated abroad`))

-- 11(2): natural person, at least 18, full legal capacity, ordinarily resident in Singapore
--                                                           natural person, age, full capacity, ordinarily resident
#ASSERT `the person qualifies as an authorised representative` (`Representative Qualification Facts` OF TRUE,  18, TRUE,  TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person qualifies as an authorised representative` (`Representative Qualification Facts` OF TRUE,  17, TRUE,  TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person qualifies as an authorised representative` (`Representative Qualification Facts` OF TRUE,  40, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person qualifies as an authorised representative` (`Representative Qualification Facts` OF TRUE,  40, TRUE,  FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person qualifies as an authorised representative` (`Representative Qualification Facts` OF FALSE, 40, TRUE,  TRUE)

-- 11(3), (4), (11): when the appointment is due
`outside Singapore at registration, business starting later` MEANS `residing outside Singapore at the time of registration` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 6 1)
`outside Singapore at registration, business starting at once` MEANS `residing outside Singapore at the time of registration` (YMD 2026 3 1) (YMD 2026 3 1)
`ceasing to reside on 1 March 2026` MEANS `ceasing to reside in Singapore after registration` (YMD 2026 3 1)
`ceasing to reside on 31 January 2026` MEANS `ceasing to reside in Singapore after registration` (YMD 2026 1 31)
`the sole authorised representative ceasing on 1 March 2026` MEANS `the sole authorised representative ceasing` (YMD 2026 3 1)

#ASSERT `the last day for appointing an authorised representative` `outside Singapore at registration, business starting later` EQUALS YMD 2026 6 1
#ASSERT `the last day for appointing an authorised representative` `outside Singapore at registration, business starting at once` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 1
#ASSERT `the last day for appointing an authorised representative` `ceasing to reside on 1 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `the last day for appointing an authorised representative` `ceasing to reside on 31 January 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 2
#ASSERT `the last day for appointing an authorised representative` `the sole authorised representative ceasing on 1 March 2026` EQUALS YMD 2026 3 31
#ASSERT `the authorised representative is appointed in time` `ceasing to reside on 1 March 2026` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the authorised representative is appointed in time` `ceasing to reside on 1 March 2026` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `the authorised representative is appointed in time` `outside Singapore at registration, business starting later` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the authorised representative is appointed in time` `outside Singapore at registration, business starting later` (YMD 2026 6 2)
#ASSERT `the authorised representative is appointed in time` `the sole authorised representative ceasing on 1 March 2026` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the authorised representative is appointed in time` `the sole authorised representative ceasing on 1 March 2026` (YMD 2026 4 1)

-- 11(4), (11): 30 days.  11(7), (9): 14 days.  The deadline is inclusive.
#TRACE `the duty to appoint an authorised representative after ceasing to reside in Singapore` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The registrant` DOES `appoint an authorised representative` AT 30

#TRACE `the duty to appoint an authorised representative after ceasing to reside in Singapore` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)

#TRACE `the duty to appoint a new authorised representative` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The registrant` DOES `appoint a new authorised representative` AT 30

#TRACE `the duty to appoint a new authorised representative` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 31)

#TRACE `the duty to lodge notice of the appointment of an authorised representative` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The registrant` DOES `lodge a notice of the appointment of, and the consent of, the authorised representative` AT 14

#TRACE `the duty to lodge notice of the appointment of an authorised representative` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 15)

#TRACE `the duty to lodge notice that an authorised representative has ceased` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `The registrant` DOES `lodge a notice that the authorised representative has ceased to be, or ceased to be qualified to be, the authorised representative` AT 14

#TRACE `the duty to lodge notice that an authorised representative has ceased` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 15)

#ASSERT `the notice of appointment contains what section 11(8) requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the notice of appointment contains what section 11(8) requires` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the notice of appointment contains what section 11(8) requires` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `the former authorised representative may lodge the notice` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the former authorised representative may lodge the notice` FALSE

-- 11(5), (6): Representative Liability Facts: date of appointment, date the obligation attached, defaulted.
#ASSERT `the authorised representative is personally responsible for the obligation` (`Representative Liability Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 1, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the authorised representative is personally responsible for the obligation` (`Representative Liability Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 4 1, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the authorised representative is personally responsible for the obligation` (`Representative Liability Facts` OF YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 2 28, FALSE)
