§§ `12. General power to cancel registration`

-- Cancellation Grounds Facts: public interest facts, Charities Act conviction, failed to appoint,
-- failed to appoint a new one, CPF Board notified.
`no ground` MEANS `Cancellation Grounds Facts` OF `no concern`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`an unlawful purpose ground` MEANS `Cancellation Grounds Facts` OF `an unlawful purpose`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a national interest ground on the Minister's certificate` MEANS `Cancellation Grounds Facts` OF `a certificate only`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a Charities Act conviction ground` MEANS `Cancellation Grounds Facts` OF `no concern`, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a failure to appoint ground` MEANS `Cancellation Grounds Facts` OF `no concern`, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`a failure to appoint a new representative ground` MEANS `Cancellation Grounds Facts` OF `no concern`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`a CPF contributions ground` MEANS `Cancellation Grounds Facts` OF `no concern`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT NOT `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` `no ground`
#ASSERT `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` `an unlawful purpose ground`
#ASSERT `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` `a national interest ground on the Minister's certificate`
#ASSERT `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` `a Charities Act conviction ground`
#ASSERT `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` `a failure to appoint ground`
#ASSERT `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` `a failure to appoint a new representative ground`
#ASSERT `there is a ground for cancellation under section 12(1) or (2)` `a CPF contributions ground`

-- 12(3): Cancellation Procedure Facts: notice given, days allowed for representations, representations considered.
#ASSERT `the procedure of section 12(3) has been followed` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF TRUE, 30, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the procedure of section 12(3) has been followed` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF TRUE, 45, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the procedure of section 12(3) has been followed` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF TRUE, 29, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the procedure of section 12(3) has been followed` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF FALSE, 30, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the procedure of section 12(3) has been followed` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF TRUE, 30, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 12` `an unlawful purpose ground` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF TRUE, 30, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 12` `an unlawful purpose ground` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF TRUE, 29, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel the registration under section 12` `no ground` (`Cancellation Procedure Facts` OF TRUE, 30, TRUE)

§§ `13. Supplemental provision to sections 9 and 12`

#ASSERT `the appeal to the Minister is excluded` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the appeal to the Minister is excluded` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the appeal to the Minister is excluded` FALSE TRUE

§§ `14. Cancellation for failure to renew registration`

-- Expiry Facts: expired, written notice given, date of notice, last day of the period stated,
-- renewed within the period, cancelled.
`expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 31 March 2026` MEANS `Expiry Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, FALSE
`expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 30 March 2026` MEANS `Expiry Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 30, FALSE, FALSE
`expired, renewed in the period` MEANS `Expiry Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, TRUE, FALSE
`expired, no notice given` MEANS `Expiry Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, FALSE
`expired and then cancelled` MEANS `Expiry Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, TRUE
`not expired` MEANS `Expiry Facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2026 3 31, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `the Registrar is to give written notice that the registration may be cancelled unless renewed` `expired, no notice given`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar is to give written notice that the registration may be cancelled unless renewed` `not expired`
#ASSERT `the period stated in the notice is long enough` `expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 31 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the period stated in the notice is long enough` `expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 30 March 2026`
#ASSERT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to renew` `expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 31 March 2026` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to renew` `expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 31 March 2026` (YMD 2026 3 31)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to renew` `expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 30 March 2026` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to renew` `expired, renewed in the period` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may cancel for failure to renew` `expired, no notice given` (YMD 2026 4 1)
#ASSERT `the person and the business name continue to be registered after expiry` `expired, notice on 1 March 2026 giving until 31 March 2026`
#ASSERT NOT `the person and the business name continue to be registered after expiry` `expired and then cancelled`
#ASSERT NOT `the person and the business name continue to be registered after expiry` `not expired`
